WEBVTT

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:12.010
What? You want to go back
for your hat and parasol?

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:16.850
Lady Dominique selected
them especially for me.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.060
No, don't be silly.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:24.560
Worst-case scenario, the Chasseurs
have already been summoned.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.230
Lady Dominique...

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:31.530
Let's go. I'll escort you to the barrier.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.940
What?

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.360
Hmm?

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:40.620
Perhaps you'd intended to stay
with me till the morning?

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:45.540
No! I can't leave without
achieving my original objective!

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.080
Original objective?

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.800
You mean determining whether
your love for me is true?

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.760
Mission accomplished, is it not?

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:55.300
Yeah, right, dream on!

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.720
I've done all this so
I'd never have to see you again!

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.350
I've worked so hard to make it happen!

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.100
I quietly suffered unbearable humiliation

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:07.980
just to pretend I was in love with--

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:09.980
Oops.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:20.490
Yes, I did find that side
of you quite lovely today.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.040
I knew that's what I liked about you.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:28.420
Huh?

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:36.840
Still, I'm surprised Luca
let you come see me alone.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.510
Are you sure it's okay?

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:43.010
Oh, you didn't tell him?

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:47.020
Master Luca is with his elder brother.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:49.150
The grand duke's brother.

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:53.980
You speak of the Bestia Loki.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:57.570
That's why I was told to take the day off

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:00.070
and received permission to come see you.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:02.700
Permission? From whom?

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:06.290
Lord Ruthven?

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:11.460
Yes. How did you...?

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.720
Vanitas?!

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:28.640
Noé!

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.070
What is it, Vanitas?

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:49.540
"The Case Study of Vanitas"

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:57.380
<i>You're pondering the simple things,</i>
<i>pretty much: human emotions, and love?</i>

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:01.760
<i>I hope one day you'll understand</i>

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.350
<i>Too many wounds have left you</i>
<i>patched together, a miserable sight</i>

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:11.600
<i>That doesn't even know</i>
<i>the definition of "alive"</i>

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:19.110
<i>No need to say,</i>
<i>"Just the two of us" or anything</i>

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:27.700
<i>I've a feeling we can understand</i>
<i>each other, and that's fine for now</i>

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:36.670
<i>I love this world,</i>
<i>and the light only you give me</i>

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:41.550
<i>Makes the world I see</i>
<i>through these fractured eyes </i>

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:46.220
<i>Look gleaming and bright</i>

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:50.810
<i>There's no such thing as a sure thing</i>

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:55.560
<i>But you can see me, can't you?</i>

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:04.410
<i>When sky and void meet, look back</i>
<i>because the dreams will come later</i>

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:33.440
Swear to me.

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:39.020
But once at the time of my choosing,

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:43.450
you shall obey my command,
no matter what it may be.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.070
Swear it.

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:48.620
Swear it!

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:59.590
I swear that...

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:04.220
...but once at the time of your choosing,

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:11.310
I shall obey your command,
no matter what it may be.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:14.180
I swear it.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.140
Excellent.

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:29.450
What? Why didn't you kill him?

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:31.620
I changed my mind.

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:33.700
The Shapeless One concerns me.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:39.500
We must discover why that monster
is keeping an Archiviste close at hand.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:43.590
Until then, it may be wiser
to use the boy as a pawn.

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:48.220
He's but a child.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:51.300
We could slay him anytime we wish.

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:56.100
I have high hopes for you, my lad.

00:05:56.100 --> 00:06:00.810
When the time comes,
do not forget your vow.

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:08.410
It's already dark outside!

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:11.530
Did I really sleep that long?!

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:17.500
Vanitas, why are you so out of breath?

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:21.250
Hmm? Have you been injured?

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:23.040
Never mind that.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:28.550
Why did Vanitas run off like that?

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:32.220
If he hasn't returned by now,

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:34.850
I suppose I can leave.

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:36.430
Jeanne.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:42.150
Professor Ruthven,
what are you doing here?

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:45.980
There was a matter that
couldn't wait to be dealt with.

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:49.450
Upon hearing a vampire had
caused an uproar on Montmartre,

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:52.160
I thought I'd come have a look.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:54.910
That was your doing, Jeanne?

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:56.950
P-Please, forgive me!

00:06:56.950 --> 00:07:01.170
I swear I didn't harm a single human!

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:05.050
Actually, I mean,
I <i>did </i>bite this one human,

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:08.510
but it was consensual!
I had their consent!

00:07:08.510 --> 00:07:11.130
Then there shall be no problem.

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:17.470
How lovely you look.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:24.110
I have no doubt Éric and Louise would
have loved to have seen you like this.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.190
Professor.

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:35.660
The night grows cold.
Come now, Jeanne, let's go home.

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:40.080
Well? Were they over there?

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:42.420
Nope, no sign of 'em.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.540
How about calling off the search?

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:48.250
It seems they made a clean escape.

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:52.680
Still, Jeanne was clearly acting strange.

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:55.470
I'll keep looking a bit longer.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:05.270
Roland!

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:09.070
Greetings, Olivier!
I can't believe you found me.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:13.530
I hear you've been sneaking around
searching for something.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:15.660
Sneaking around? That's not nice.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:19.580
I'm simply brushing up on my history.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:20.700
History?

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:22.080
That's right.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:25.420
The history of humans
and vampires, to be precise.

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.000
No need to look so angry.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.970
I haven't laid a hand on
any of the forbidden tomes.

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:35.840
Why do this now?

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:40.270
I thought I might find something
unlike anything before.

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:47.270
I had always thought
of vampires as pure evil.

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:52.860
Of that, I had no doubt.
I had no grounds to question it.

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:55.320
But I've learned that's not true!

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:57.120
My eyes are open!

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:01.410
There is no cause for concern.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:08.340
One so deeply faithful as Captain Roland
would never do harm to the Church.

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:10.710
You do not understand, Georges.

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:15.430
Strictly speaking,
it is not God he believes in.

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:19.430
He believes in <i>himself</i>
as one of the Lord's faithful.

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:26.310
You listen to me, Roland!

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:31.110
You are a Chasseur, a hunter
of vampires in our Lord's name!

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:35.150
If our superiors learn of such remarks,
you'll be deemed dangerous.

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:40.620
And if worst comes to worst, your parents
and siblings may come to harm!

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:50.290
Say, Olivier.

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:54.420
How many paladins do you
think I could battle on my own?

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:55.470
What?

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:57.300
Three? Four?

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:00.140
Maybe even more if I wanted to tempt fate?

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:01.550
What is this nonsense?!

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:03.140
Oh, but...

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:07.230
I imagine I'd be
hard-pressed if I battled you.

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:14.610
After all that, he has
the nerve to threaten <i>me</i>?

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:18.700
You understand, Olivier?

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:21.320
You know what kind of man I am.

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:28.540
I can only believe in that
which I believe to be true.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:33.840
Hell's bells.

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:37.510
What is this?

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:38.340
Quack!

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:39.550
Dante.

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:41.640
Dominique's not with you?

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:42.850
What? Domi?

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:45.560
Aw, hell. I thought you might be on to us.

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:48.850
Anyone who didn't notice that
needs their head examined.

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:51.190
I won't argue that.

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:55.360
But enough about that, quack!
Some unbelievable info just came in!

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:57.400
The Beast lives!

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:59.610
The Beast of Gévaudan

00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:02.990
has reared its head!

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:07.120
Gévau... what?

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:09.040
Now that's interesting.

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:13.080
Don't spare the details, Dante.

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:20.510
It is said to have
resembled an enormous wolf.

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:23.470
Its large maw was twisted,
and its ears pointed.

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:27.520
It had sharp claws and
a body covered in red fur.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:32.850
And it had many
black stripes upon its back.

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:35.900
The 18th-century regions
of Auvergne and Gévaudan

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:41.320
were where over 100 women and
children were brutally ripped to shreds.

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:48.660
Known as the Beast of Gévaudan,
it had the people cowering in fear.

00:11:55.250 --> 00:12:00.470
Even now, there are all sorts of theories
as to what the Beast really was.

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:04.840
But back then, both Church
and vampires agreed on one thing.

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:11.310
The Beast of Gévaudan was none
other than a curse-bearing vampire!

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:20.990
So what's this about the
Beast of Gévaudan rearing its head?

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:24.990
Is it truly the same Beast
as the 18th-century killer?

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:28.240
Honestly, I can't say either way yet.

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:32.210
But five bodies have
already turned up this month.

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:37.170
All the killings differed. Some had their
entrails devoured or heads torn off.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:40.340
Just like in the 18th century, eh?

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:44.630
Yeah, and there are even
eyewitness accounts of the Beast.

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:47.470
So? What's the plan, quack?

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:54.100
I'll go see for myself
whether it really is a curse-bearer.

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:59.110
What will you do, Noé?

00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:02.780
Who? Me?

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:05.070
Let me think.

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:09.240
I... umm...

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:13.710
I think it sounds truly delicious.

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:15.920
Huh?

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:19.130
Delicious? You don't
mean the Beast, do you?

00:13:19.130 --> 00:13:23.130
I didn't see that one coming.

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:28.800
Don't tell me you have some
kind of creepy food fetish.

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:31.680
This is bad, bad. Really bad.

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:36.350
Vanitas's blood smells so good.
I can't focus on the conversation.

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:41.820
It doesn't make sense.
I already knew how good it smelled.

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:44.690
Why do I feel this way?

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:46.070
I'm starving!

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:48.700
I slept the entire day away.

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:51.240
Which means I haven't eaten anything!

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:54.120
Which means I'm absolutely ravenous!

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:56.210
Yes, that must be it!

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:59.710
When I'm hungry,
I always get thirsty, too!

00:13:59.710 --> 00:14:03.550
So it's because I slept too much.
I do feel really lethargic.

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:12.510
Damn it. It feels like my sense
of smell is only getting stronger.

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:16.140
His blood smells positively delectable.
I must have a taste.

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:19.190
No, wait! I should have
some bread or something first.

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:20.230
I want blood.

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:24.650
I know, but we're in the midst
of an important conversation.

00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:29.820
Wait. Is it all right to suck the blood of
a human that has been marked?

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:31.280
It smells so sweet.

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:35.790
Just a taste will do. He must let me try.

00:14:35.790 --> 00:14:36.910
What's with him?

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:39.080
Beats me.

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:44.500
This is like the time I sucked the blood
of that village child just for fun.

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:48.380
Listen well, Mon Chaton.

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:54.010
You have the power to see people's
memories by sucking their blood.

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:58.310
That means you have to be
more careful than other vampires.

00:14:58.310 --> 00:14:59.890
So then...

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:04.610
In other words, he means blood-sucking
is a form of communication.

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:06.860
So if you thirst for someone's blood,

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:10.410
you must coax them
into letting you have it.

00:15:11.490 --> 00:15:13.530
Coax them?!

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:16.750
What? How am I supposed to do that?!

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:21.210
Noé, what's gotten into--

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:26.670
Vanitas! Your blood has a divine aroma
that one would not imagine possible

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:30.880
given your intolerable
personality and attitude.

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:33.140
Huh? Are you picking a fight?

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:35.390
It's a compliment!

00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:39.060
So, in other words,

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:41.770
what I'm trying to say is...

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:43.770
Vanitas! I want but a taste of your--

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:45.320
Archiviste!

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:50.650
I'll say this but once, so listen well.

00:15:53.410 --> 00:15:59.540
If you make any attempt to suck my blood
and thereby peer into my memories,

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:01.080
I will kill you.

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:04.130
Is that clear?

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:09.800
Yes.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:12.930
Please forgive me.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:40.250
I sure bungled that.

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:45.710
You have it all wrong.

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:50.300
I didn't want to peer into your memories.

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:57.300
Then again, is that really true?

00:17:00.970 --> 00:17:03.350
Maybe <i>I'm </i>wrong.

00:17:08.270 --> 00:17:10.190
I...

00:18:20.970 --> 00:18:22.890
Just stop it already.

00:18:22.890 --> 00:18:24.680
You're knocking me off-kilter.

00:18:24.680 --> 00:18:27.940
If you've a bone to pick
with me, out with it!

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:32.440
No, it's nothing like that.

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:37.490
I wanted to say that what happened
yesterday was all my fault.

00:18:38.530 --> 00:18:45.000
Truth be told, part of me
wants to blame you

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:47.750
for emitting such a sickly
sweet scent around a vampire.

00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:48.620
Watch it!

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:52.750
But if I had to say, I can't
swear that sucking your blood

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:57.670
wasn't a pretext born of my desire
to get a glimpse of your past.

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:03.180
Why even bother peering into my past?

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:06.730
What would you gain from that?

00:19:06.730 --> 00:19:11.810
I don't know what I would gain and
whatnot, but I did once say to you,

00:19:11.810 --> 00:19:15.480
"I do find you intriguing."

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:24.330
Does that Archiviste power of yours
let you see memories in people's blood,

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:26.750
no matter the source?

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:30.710
No, it's just like draining life energy.

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:37.510
You must suck the blood from their veins
if you wish to delve into their memories.

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:46.060
With other sources, I may,
in rare cases, see fragments of emotions.

00:19:46.060 --> 00:19:47.640
I see.

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:53.440
In that case, the next time I'm injured,
you can lap up the blood on my clothes.

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:55.570
But that's a one-time offer.

00:19:55.570 --> 00:19:57.400
What?! Really?!

00:19:57.400 --> 00:19:58.230
Just kidding.

00:19:58.230 --> 00:20:00.150
What?!

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:13.250
All right, let's go, Noé.

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:16.880
Okay!

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:27.260
We'll take this to Gévaudan.

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:29.720
This?!

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:39.820
Pardon me.

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:41.110
No need.

00:20:41.110 --> 00:20:45.870
It was entirely my fault, monsieur.

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:47.660
Noé, over here.

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:51.750
Wait for me, Vanitas!

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:57.960
I-I'm so sleepy.

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:00.590
You haven't slept a wink?

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:08.010
I was sure that you would go off and
abandon me when I wasn't looking.

00:21:08.010 --> 00:21:13.520
We have a long way to go.
You'd best get some sleep while you can.

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:17.480
If I fall asleep...

00:21:17.480 --> 00:21:21.990
...you're not going to leave me?

00:21:21.990 --> 00:21:25.030
I'll wake you when we're there.

00:21:25.030 --> 00:21:25.740
Now get some sleep.

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:27.200
"Point of Departure"

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:27.200
Now get some sleep.

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:27.990
"Point of Departure"

00:23:26.530 --> 00:23:29.990
At last, the time has come.

00:23:29.990 --> 00:23:32.820
Here in Gévaudan,

00:23:32.820 --> 00:23:37.370
I shall make my song of vengeance
echo across the land.

